    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n22674" root="شفو and شفى" body-key="$">
    
      2 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شفّاهُ بِكُلِ شَىْءٍ</span></b> , inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَشْفِيَةٌ</span>, <i>He treated
him medically,</i> or <i>curatively, with everything
whereby he might attain recovery,</i> or <i>restoration
to convalescence.</i> (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَا شَفَّى فُلَانٌ أَفْضَلُ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مِمَّا شَفَّيْتَ</span> i. e. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَا ٱزْدَادَ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَبِحَ</span> [meaning <i>The
gain of such a one</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ما</span> being here what is termed
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَصْدَرِيَّة</span>, as <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اِزْدَادَ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَبِحَ</span> are intrans.,) <i>is more
excellent than thy gain</i>] is said to be an instance
of substitution, [originally <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَفَّفَ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَفَّفْتَ</span>,] like
[<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَصَّى</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَقَصَّى</span> and] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَقَضَّى</span> [for <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَصَّصَ</span> and
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَقَصَّصَ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَقَضَّضَ</span>]. (TA.)

